# Architecture Rules

This is ESP32 firmware with a documented baseline architecture — see `docs/adr/ADR-0002-project-architecture-baseline.md` and `.ai/architecture-summary.md`.

- Boot/runtime is a linear FreeRTOS task chain, single core, flag-polling for cross-task signaling (the only queue is the I2C sniffer's ISR event queue). Don't introduce RTOS queues for task-to-task messaging without a superseding ADR (`docs/adr/ADR-0004-freertos-linear-task-chain.md`).
- Hardware/network/RF/I2C access goes through the existing global manager singletons (`main/managers/*`, e.g. `rfManager`, `i2cManager`) — don't construct a new instance of an existing manager class.
- Itho device support is a data table (`ithoDevices[]` in `main/ithodevice/IthoDevice.cpp`) — add a device via a new row + label header in `main/ithodevice/devices/`, not a subclass.
- REST v2 keeps business logic in framework-agnostic `processXxx` functions (`main/api/WebAPIv2.cpp`) separate from `AsyncWebServer` routing (`handleXxx` in `main/api/WebAPIv2Rest.cpp`). MQTT command handling (`main/api/MqttAPI.cpp`) reuses the same `processXxx` logic — never duplicate validation.
- Never edit `software/lib/*` (vendored libraries) or hand-edit `main/webroot/*_gz.h` (generated by `build_script.py`).

Any change to one of these baseline facts is architecturally significant — require a spec (`specs/templates/`) and check/update the matching ADR (`docs/adr/README.md` trigger table) before implementing.
